Bob Blunt <RobertDOTblunt@digitalDOTcom> writes:

>console.  If you toss a new SCSI drive into a VAX without power cycling, 
>you typically have to go thru a cycle of HALT, UNJAM and INIT for the 
>device to show up properly to the console before it shows up with SHOW 
>DEVICE.  In my experience the same has held true for most all Alpha 
>consoles with direct-connected SCSI devices.

That hasn't been my experience at all.  The console appears to poll the
SCSI bus once every couple of minutes.  If I add a SCSI drive to an alpha
sitting at the >>> prompt it appears but not immediately.  Same if I
remove one, it disappears but not immediately.  Also if you have a SCSI
cluster with one system on the shared bus booted and the other at the
console prompt, you'll see periodic mount verifys, apparently when the
system at the console prompt polls the SCSI bus and does something to
upset the VMS system.

Of course this probably depends on what model Alpha and the console 
firmware version.


