> and each of the two batteries in those units used 3 of the same cells
> soldered onto a PC board.  They are hot-glued into the plastic shells,
> so I'm lucky mine are still good (for now) but at least I know where to
> get the cells.
> 

   They just keep making it harder and harder to replace the batteries,
don't they?. With the Raid Array 8000 it was just 2 batteries and a
bit of wire. With the MA2200 there were more wires and a small circuit
board inside the battery pack. I guess it is understandable that
HP doesn't want you to be able to rebuild the battery packs when they
charge about $1000 for $16 worth of batteries, a couple of wires,
a connector and some shrink wrap.



