I think it will depend mostly on what your workload is, and how you
have the drives arranged into storage units.  Mirror sets?  Stripes?
Combination/raid?

One customer a long time ago upgraded from HSZ50/KZPSA to HSZ70/KZPBA
and reported well over 2X performance boost using the same drive
configurations.  They got another 10-15% when they swapped out the old
7200RPM drives for 10Krpm 18GB drives later.  I don't have any info on
the storage unit setups they used.

Keep an eye open for the differential KZPBA-CB (I think thats the
correct p/n) as it will make a substantial difference in performance
with HSZ70/80 units over a KZPSA.

Rich



