Last week, I pulled out a TF85 drive from a DSSI enclosure.  No problem.

But when I put the unit back it, the whole cabinet powered off. I have
to pysically move the power switch to OFF for a while and then power the
cabinet back up.

Seems that the power su0pply detected an anomaly/short when I inserted
the tape drive into the DSSI slot and shut down. The power supply had no
fault indication on it. But fans were off.

If you have a compressor, try blowing air into each backpane connector
to ensure there is no "lint" that could short the power leads. 

Did you manage to pull out ALL boards from the system and try to power
it up to see if the power supply is then happy ? And then put back each
board one by one until a fault happens ?


