This sounds like a problem I had with a couple of PDP11/44's.  I thought
it was bad power supplies but it turned out to be the DC OK detection
circuit on the CIM.  By disabling this I was able to boot and run the
systems just fine. (After testing the PS with a scope to be sure it really
was working properly.)

bill

