> How do you format a hard drive in SRM. I'm trying to install openvms on
> an AlphaStation 600. But I can't install it until I format the drive. A
> show dev command shows the single internal scsi hard drive fine. Will
> the openvms cd allow me to format the hard drive before installing the
> system on the hard drive?

   What exactly do you mean by "can't install it until I format the drive"?

   OpenVMS doesn't have that particular requirement on any SCSI or IDE/ATA disk 
device I've encountered, and the installation off the CD generally deals with 
this for you entirely transparently.  Just install OpenVMS on the disk.

   From this, I might easily infer that you have an unsupported disk, or a bus 
error or some other hardware problem or configuration issue arising here, and 
that you've seen some sort of error messages and/or an unsupported device and/or 
unsupported version for the configuration, or some other sort of error.

   Would you mind posting additional details around what you have?  What would 
be the OpenVMS Alpha version, the particulars of the target system disk device 
and the related I/O configuration, error message text, what installation 
operation(s) and/or command(s) have you tried, etc.


