>> anybody have an opinion which OS is better suited for this machine. My
>> experience is mostly with SGI machines. Would greatly appreciate any
>> advice.
>
> I have no OpenVMS experience, but at my work we used a similar machine
> for more than 10 years as one of the most imortant machines running
> a heterogeneous network. The latter 5 years it ran DU v3.2G with no
> problems at all. It was also our ntp server for all these years.
> Nice hardware, install, read "man advfs" and be enjoy!
>
> Kjell

You could run either, I run both on various Alphas but prefer VMS.  One
problem you may encounter is updating the firmware, e.g., I can't get a  
late
enough version on my XP1000s to run wwidmgr so updating Fibre Channel HBAs
I have to use something later like DS10L (very good buy, BTW, see  
islandco.com)
or ES40s.  Later version of VMS have some very nifty features, shadowing,
load balancing, et. al., If you run Tru64 I would go for 5.1 and later

